        "root_concepts": "[filters]",
        "section": "electronics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "03 - Filters",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │          |H(jω)| (dB)                                               │\n  │   0 ──────────────────                                              │\n  │                          ╲                                          │\n  │  -Rp (ripple) ─ ─ ─ ─ ─  ╲ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─                                │\n  │                              ╲ transition                           │\n  │  -As (stopband) ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─  ╲─────────── ─ ─ ─                     │\n  │                   ωp     ωs        ω                                │\n  │            passband  stopband edge                                  │\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-FILTERS.md#009",
      "path": [
        "03-FILTERS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:electronics:03-filters, git-history:electronics:03-filters]",
        "canonical_path": "electronics/03-FILTERS.md",
        "concepts": "[filters]",
        "current_path": "electronics/03-FILTERS.md",
        "id": "maxim:electronics:filters",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "electronics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[filters]",
        "section": "electronics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "03 - Filters",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Key specs:\n    ωp = passband edge frequency (where attenuation = Rp dB)\n    ωs = stopband edge frequency (where attenuation ≥ As dB)\n    Rp = passband ripple (typically 0.1–3 dB)\n    As = stopband attenuation (typically 20–80 dB)\n    Selectivity: ωs/ωp (closer to 1 = harder)"
    },
